1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,210
Section 1

2
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:02,180
LINDA:

3
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:04,220
Hello, Linda speaking.

4
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,323
MATT:

5
00:00:05,323 --> 00:00:06,145
Oh hi, Linda.

6
00:00:06,145 --> 00:00:07,269
This is Matt Brooks.

7
00:00:07,269 --> 00:00:09,555
Alex White gave me your number.

8
00:00:09,555 --> 00:00:14,890
He said you'd be able to give me some advice about moving to Banford.

9
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:15,467
LINDA:

10
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:18,352
Yes, Alex did mention you.

11
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:20,660
How can I help?

12
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:21,146
MATT:

13
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:25,520
Well, first of all - which area to live in?

14
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:26,126
LINDA:

15
00:00:26,126 --> 00:00:29,155
Well, I live in Dalton,

16
00:00:29,155 --> 00:00:34,001
which is a really nice suburb-not too expensive,

17
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:37,030
and there's a nice park.

18
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:37,373
MATT:

19
00:00:37,373 --> 00:00:38,060
Sounds good.

20
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:42,867
Do you know how much it would be to rent a two bedroom flat

21
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:43,210
there?

22
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:43,782
LINDA:

23
00:00:43,782 --> 00:00:51,789
Yeah, you should be able to get something reasonable for 850 pounds per month.

24
00:00:51,789 --> 00:00:54,649
That's what people typically pay.

25
00:00:54,649 --> 00:01:00,368
You certainly wouldn't want to pay more than 900 pounds.

26
00:01:00,368 --> 00:01:03,800
That doesn't include bills or anything.

27
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,252
MATT:

28
00:01:04,252 --> 00:01:04,704
No.

29
00:01:04,704 --> 00:01:06,060
That sounds alright.

30
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,772
I'll definitely have a look there.

31
00:01:08,772 --> 00:01:12,840
Are the transport links easy from where you live?

32
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:13,346
LINDA:

33
00:01:13,346 --> 00:01:15,368
Well, I'm very lucky.

34
00:01:15,368 --> 00:01:22,447
I work in the city centre so I don't have to use public transport.

35
00:01:22,447 --> 00:01:24,470
I go by bike.

36
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:24,824
MATT:

37
00:01:24,824 --> 00:01:27,300
Oh, I wish I could do that.

38
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,130
Is it safe to cycle around the city?

39
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:30,702
LINDA:

40
00:01:30,702 --> 00:01:32,419
Yes, it's fine.

41
00:01:32,419 --> 00:01:35,280
And it keeps me fit.

42
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:42,147
Anyway, driving to work in the city centre would be a nightmare

43
00:01:42,147 --> 00:01:45,008
because there's hardly any parking.

44
00:01:45,008 --> 00:01:50,730
And the traffic during the rush hour can be bad.

45
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:51,065
MATT:

46
00:01:51,065 --> 00:01:55,424
I'd be working from home but I'd have to go to London one

47
00:01:55,424 --> 00:01:57,100
or two days a week.

48
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:57,745
LINDA:

49
00:01:57,745 --> 00:01:58,391
Oh,

50
00:01:58,391 --> 00:01:59,682
that's perfect.

51
00:01:59,682 --> 00:02:03,555
Getting to London is no problem.

52
00:02:03,555 --> 00:02:11,300
There's a fast train every 30 minutes which only takes 45 minutes.

53
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:11,873
MATT:

54
00:02:11,873 --> 00:02:13,020
That's good.

55
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:13,558
LINDA:

56
00:02:13,558 --> 00:02:18,404
Yeah, the train service isn't bad during the week.

57
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:22,172
And they run quite late at night.

58
00:02:22,172 --> 00:02:25,402
It's weekends that are a problem.

59
00:02:25,402 --> 00:02:32,939
They're always doing engineering work and you have to take a bus to Hadham

60
00:02:32,939 --> 00:02:36,170
and pick up the train there,

61
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:38,323
which is really slow.

62
00:02:38,323 --> 00:02:43,707
But other than that, Banford's a great place to live.

63
00:02:43,707 --> 00:02:45,860
I've never been happier.

64
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:46,318
LINDA:

65
00:02:46,318 --> 00:02:52,730
There are some nice restaurants in the city centre and a brand new cinema

66
00:02:52,730 --> 00:02:56,852
which has only been open a couple of months.

67
00:02:56,852 --> 00:02:59,600
There's a good arts centre too.

68
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,051
MATT:

69
00:03:00,051 --> 00:03:02,760
Sounds like Banford's got it all.

70
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:03,272
LINDA:

71
00:03:03,272 --> 00:03:03,783
Yes!

72
00:03:03,783 --> 00:03:05,318
We're really lucky.

73
00:03:05,318 --> 00:03:10,433
There are lots of really good aspects to living here.

74
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:17,595
The schools are good and the hospital here is one of the best in

75
00:03:17,595 --> 00:03:18,618
the country.

76
00:03:18,618 --> 00:03:23,734
Everyone I know who's been there's had a positive experience.

77
00:03:23,734 --> 00:03:30,895
Oh, I can give you the name of my dentist too in Bridge Street,

78
00:03:30,895 --> 00:03:32,430
if you're interested.

79
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:39,080
I've been going to him for years and I've never had any problems.

80
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:39,860
MATT:

81
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:41,420
Oh, OK.

82
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,200
Thanks!

83
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:42,635
LINDA:

84
00:03:42,635 --> 00:03:46,550
I'll find his number and send it to you.

85
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:47,057
MATT:

86
00:03:47,057 --> 00:03:47,564
Thanks,

87
00:03:47,564 --> 00:03:50,100
that would be really helpful.

88
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:50,592
LINDA:

89
00:03:50,592 --> 00:03:54,040
Are you planning to visit Banford soon?

90
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:54,440
MATT:

91
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:54,840
Yes.

92
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:58,440
My wife and I are both coming next week.

93
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:02,040
We want to make some appointments with estate agents.

94
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:02,418
LINDA:

95
00:04:02,418 --> 00:04:06,570
I could meet you if you like and show you around.

96
00:04:06,570 --> 00:04:07,078
MATT:

97
00:04:07,078 --> 00:04:08,600
Are you sure?

98
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,630
We'd really appreciate that.

99
00:04:10,630 --> 00:04:11,201
LINDA:

100
00:04:11,201 --> 00:04:18,050
Either a Tuesday or Thursday is good for me, after 5.30.

101
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:18,603
MATT:

102
00:04:18,603 --> 00:04:24,680
Thursday's preferable - Tuesday I need to get home before 6 pm.

103
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:25,263
LINDA:

104
00:04:25,263 --> 00:04:25,846
OK.

105
00:04:25,846 --> 00:04:26,430
Great.

106
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:34,595
Let me know which train you're catching and I'll meet you in the cafe

107
00:04:34,595 --> 00:04:35,178
outside.

108
00:04:35,178 --> 00:04:37,511
You can't miss it.

109
00:04:37,511 --> 00:04:42,760
It's opposite the station and next to the museum.

110
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,289
MATT:

111
00:04:43,289 --> 00:04:43,819
Brilliant.

112
00:04:43,819 --> 00:04:46,995
I'll text you next week then.

113
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:50,700
Thanks so much for all the advice.

114
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:51,211
LINDA:

115
00:04:51,211 --> 00:04:52,234
No problem.

116
00:04:52,234 --> 00:04:54,790
I'll see you next week.
